(*
env: OEVM_NO_NTP=1
expect:
sync failed nil
still ringing
finished
*)
(* tuvm#94 stage 4 — a failed sync answers nil, and the node must read that as
   "keep free-running", not as an error.

   OEVM_NO_NTP (src/platform.c) forces the failure path, delivered PER-TEST via the
   env: header so it cannot leak into 05's has-seconds assertion -- a global export
   would silently turn that test's arithmetic into a nil-dereference.

   The second line is the actual claim. Answering nil is only half of the contract;
   the other half is that nil is an ORDINARY answer, so a node can branch on it with
   no handler in sight. If this seam ever grows a raise, this test stops compiling
   its way to `still ringing` and that is the intended alarm -- the failure would
   otherwise surface as a clock that stops ringing when the WiFi drops, which is the
   exact opposite of what the rung promises. *)
class NtpNoSync packageUsing: manifest = () (
  public main: platform args: args = (
    | secs |
    secs:: platform ntpSyncTz: -25200.
    secs == nil
      ifTrue:  [ 'sync failed nil' out ]
      ifFalse: [ ('sync did NOT fail: ' , secs printString) out ].

    (* No handler anywhere above or below: reaching this line at all is the proof
       that a missed sync is an answer and not a raise. *)
    'still ringing' out.
    'finished' out.
  )
) : (
)
